<title>BELGIUM: EU delays decision on Argentine flint maize.</title>
<headline>EU delays decision on Argentine flint maize.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union cereals experts group postponed a decision on Argentine flint maize import duties on Thursday to give member states time to assess proposals, an EU official said on Friday.</p>
<p>A decision by the European Council to reduce import duties by eight Ecus from 14 Ecus has yet to be implemented.</p>
<p>&quot;The experts group will return to the issues in about two weeks time and there will be two votes,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The cereals management committee may be asked to vote first on a regulation allowing reimbursement of duty paid between January 1, when the reduction should have come into force, and June 1996.</p>
<p>A second vote will be put establishing the reduction from July 1 1996. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
